L= 40: ADePM 17 iters vs DePM 54 iters to eps=1e-03  -> speedup 3.18x  (comm ratio ADePM/DePM = 0.315, i.e. ADePM uses less total communication for the SAME accuracy target)
L= 80: ADePM 17 iters vs DePM 54 iters to eps=1e-03  -> speedup 3.18x  (comm ratio ADePM/DePM = 0.315, i.e. ADePM uses less total communication for the SAME accuracy target)

At small L the one-shot averaging methods (ADePM, DePM) may fail to reach a tight target at all (insufficient consensus per PCA step), while DeEPCA's gradient-tracking makes its accuracy asymptotically L-independent -- this is expected and matches the paper's Table 2 characterization (ADePM/DePM require L = Omega(1/sqrt(gamma_W) log(.)); DeEPCA does not).

Total runtime: 11.8s
